    "title": "Why This Oklahoma Museum Feels Like Time Travel - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Elowen Frost ,\n11 hours ago Nestled along the historic Route 66 in Clinton, Oklahoma, the Oklahoma Route 66 Museum at 2229 W Gary Blvd stands as a portal to America’s most beloved highway. This remarkable museum captures the spirit of the Mother Road through decades of carefully preserved artifacts, vintage displays, and immersive exhibits that transport visitors back to the golden age of American road travel. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
